{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Hamiltonian path, or nil when there is none (or no vertex): the first one a depth-first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"backtracking search finds, from each vertex in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, extending through each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" in order to an unvisited vertex (Mathematica"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FindHamiltonianPath"},{"type":"text","text":"). Self-loops never help; one vertex is the trivial path. Pruning cuts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only subtrees with no solution (an unvisited vertex unreachable, or left with too few"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"usable neighbours), so it keeps the order. Without a start the search is run again from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each vertex in turn until one succeeds, so a graph with no Hamiltonian path costs n"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"searches."}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"hamiltonianPath","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Path","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Walks\/documentation\/Walks\/Path","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks4PathV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocol